{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "71b8a04c-91c4-886a-bf96-abec3228f2d3",
  "created_at": "2026-01-16T10:43:16-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Zoning and Inspections",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Deirdre Quinn",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Greg Lombardi",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:39:18-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Zoning and Inspections, this is Greg."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:39:21-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good morning, Greg. Please excuse me, I hope I am calling the right office. I have a question about a fence."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:39:29-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're in the right place. What's the question?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:39:33-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you. My neighbor is putting up a fence now, they have the workers there this week, and I would like to do the same on my side. Please, can you tell me if I need a permit for this?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:39:48-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Generally, yes, a fence needs a permit. What kind of fence are you thinking, and how tall?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:39:55-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Excuse me, one moment. [pause] Sorry. It is composite, the material that is not wood. And six feet tall. I think six feet is what my neighbor has also."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:40:06-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Composite, six feet. That's on the taller side, so you'd want to go through the permit process for that."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:40:14-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I see. Please, I want to ask, is there a height where the fence does not need a permit anymore? Like, if I make it smaller, maybe four feet, then I do not need the paper?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:40:27-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I wouldn't count on that. Shorter fences can still need a permit, so don't assume a lower one lets you skip it. The safe thing is to apply before you build anything."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:40:39-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ah, okay. So the height does not decide if I need the permit. It decides only what kind of fence I can have. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:40:49-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sort of. The height matters for what's allowed, but the permit question is separate. Plan on needing one either way."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:40:57-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, I understand a little. Thank you. And please, another question. Do I have to tell my neighbor before I build? Or the city tells them?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:41:07-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The city doesn't send out a notice for a regular fence, as far as I know. Being a good neighbor, you'd probably want to let them know yourself, especially if it's near the property line. Do you know where your line is?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:41:22-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Um, not exactly. I have the papers from when we bought the house, maybe there is a drawing. Do I need to know this for the permit?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:41:32-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, you'll need to show where the fence goes on your lot. If you have a survey or plot plan from the closing, bring a copy. That helps a lot."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:41:43-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, I will look for it. Excuse me, one more thing, my phone is making noise. It is the school calendar application, it keeps sending me the same reminder two and three times. I am sorry."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:41:56-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem, happens to all of us. Take your time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:42:00-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you, it stopped. So, I find the drawing, and then I come to the office to ask for the permit form?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:42:08-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You can stop by City Hall, or the application can be picked up there. Bring the plot plan, a sketch of the fence, and the material and height you told me. Staff at the counter can walk you through it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:42:23-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Please, one question more, so I am sure. The permit is for the fence on my side only, not for my neighbor's fence?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:42:32-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, yours only. Their fence is their own application."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:42:36-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. And if my neighbor did not get a permit, is that a problem for me?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:42:42-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Not for you. Just focus on yours. If you're worried about theirs, I can note the address, and someone can look into it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:42:51-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, no, thank you, I only wanted to know. I am still a little confused about the height, but I think I will ask again at the counter with the drawing."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:43:02-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's fine. Bring the drawing and they'll sort out the height with you. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:43:08-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, that is all. Thank you very much for your patience, Greg. Have a good day."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-16T10:43:14-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too. Take care."
    }
  ],
